      },
      "content": "# Key Findings\n\n· Demand for behavior analysts continues to grow. Annual nationwide demand for individuals\nholding BCBA or BCBA-D certification has increased each year since 2010, with a 28% increase\nfrom 2024 to 2025. Demand was highest in five states in 2025 (ordered from most to least):\nCalifornia, New Jersey, Texas, Massachusetts, and North Carolina. These five states account for\n38% of the recent demand for behavior analysts, with California alone accounting for 15% of the\n2025 demand.\n\n· The demand for assistant behavior analysts decreased in 2025. After a significant 131%\nincrease in demand from 2023 to 2024, the demand for BCaBA certification decreased\nbetween 2024 and 2025; however, there is still an overall increasing trend for BCaBA\ncertification demand since 2010. Demand was highest in five states in 2025 (ordered from\nmost to least): California, Florida, Michigan, Texas, and Pennsylvania. These five states account\nfor 43% of the recent demand for assistant behavior analysts, with California alone accounting\nfor 15% of the 2025 demand.\n\n<!-- PageFooter=\"Updated 01/2026\" -->\n<!-- PageNumber=\"- 1 -\" -->\n<!-- PageFooter=\"@ 2026, BACB® | All rights reserved\" -->\n<!-- PageBreak -->\n\n<!-- PageHeader=\"2010-2025\" -->\n<!-- PageHeader=\"US EMPLOYMENT DEMAND FOR BEHAVIOR ANALYSTS\" -->",
